<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX3-QA3-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX3-QA3-001" ;
  triage:title "composition_installs_the_task_store removes its temp dir while the SQLite runtime assembly is still alive; fails on Windows CI with a sharing violation (os error 32)" ;
  triage:description "Found by CI on PR #1191 head 95f05b3f7f3106a67826383530f476693d0c3e6c: job 'Test (windows-latest)' of run 33958891979 failed with exactly one test failure, composition::tests::composition_installs_the_task_store in crates/atm-runtime/src/composition.rs, panicking at line 348 col 39 with 'remove tempdir: Os { code: 32, ... The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process. }'. The test (added for AX3-QA2-003 in commit 95f05b3f7) creates a temp dir under std::env::temp_dir(), opens an isolated SQLite boundary via atm_runtime_test_support::open_isolated_sqlite_boundary(&root), asserts task_store().is_ok(), then calls std::fs::remove_dir_all(root).expect(...) while assembly (and its reader-pool/writer threads holding the .sqlite files open) is still in scope. On Windows an open file cannot be deleted, so the cleanup panics. ubuntu and macos passed. rust-qa-agent flagged the manual temp-dir cleanup as a minor note in ax3-qa-r3; it is a real cross-platform defect (docs/cross-platform-guidelines.md). Fix: drop the assembly before cleanup (drop(assembly)) and prefer tempfile::TempDir bound before the assembly so drop order releases the files first, or skip manual removal entirely; apply the same hygiene to daemon_config_doctor_does_not_read_a_caller_workspace only if it has the same pattern with an open handle. This blocks the merge gate because CI must be green at merge time. Crate-wide sweep (sweep_scope=crate, crates/atm-runtime) at HEAD 95f05b3f7f3106a67826383530f476693d0c3e6c found exactly 2 remove_dir_all call sites, both in composition.rs: line 348 (this finding) has a live SQLite runtime/storage handle (assembly) still in scope at the call, confirmed open; line 377 in daemon_config_doctor_does_not_read_a_caller_workspace removes a plain fixture workspace directory with no open storage/runtime handle (RuntimeConfigDoctor holds no file handle on the directory), so it is assessed as not exhibiting this defect pattern and is not recorded as a confirmed occurrence." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "CI" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T12:10:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Blocking finding closed by a later valid Completion and quality-mgr follow-up QA; final sprint verdict AX3-QA7 PASS 0/0/0 (PR #1191 comment 5551705615)." ;
